-- Minmatar COSMOS briefings from the client localization
-- +migrate Up

UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Well, it''s rather complicated. But to keep it simple, I''ll give you the short version. A few days ago, I completed my latest project, the ST 50 series. They were supposed to be ultra-intelligent fighter drones, specifically ordered by the Minmatar Fleet to serve in our armed forces. In all of the tests I performed on them, they seemed to be in fine condition, easily dispatching all the previous models in our combat simulation tests. However, shortly after they were released from our lab and sent into action, they went missing. The loss was an enormous blow to Boundless Creation, especially considering all the time, effort, and money we spent creating those things. 
The sortie that they were on when they went missing was to attack a massive rogue drone hive within Barkrik. They were accompanied by over a dozen human pilots, who also haven''t been seen since. I''m not sure exactly what happened there, but a rumor is spreading that they were overwhelmed and captured by the rogue drone mothership. I can''t imagine such a thing happening, but... 
Anyway, a few days later we heard of a terrible tragedy in Hjoramold. An entire settlement was destroyed by rampaging rogue drones. I didn''t think much of it at the time, considering rogue drone attacks are pretty frequent in these parts, but later that day I turned on the evening news I heard something that chilled me to the bone. The recent rogue drone attacks were led by none other than one of my own ST drones! I couldn''t believe my ears at first, but it was true. I don''t know how, but the rogue drones have somehow managed to reconfigure the ST''s AI chip and turn it into a rampaging monster! It must be stopped at all costs; its existence is a terrible blow to my career, and the more damage it causes, the more likely I am to lose my job. You must help me! 
Unfortunately, the rogues seem to have deactivated the tracking devices I had installed into the STs. However, I have managed to triangulate the location of two of them, and the third has already been destroyed by local independent capsuleers. You''ll find ST 58 at the bookmarked location that I''m about to upload into your NeoCom, floating around a deadspace pocket filled with asteroids. Please bring back its memory chip so that I can study it and find out what went wrong.' WHERE missionID=93401 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I came here to ask the Sisters for help in a quest I''m on, but they refused. They said my situation wasn''t dire enough. But what do they know? This is a matter of the utmost importance to me and my family clan. It''s hard for those not directly involved to understand my plight, I guess. But let my attempt to explain it adequately to you.
For generations my family clan has been the guardian of the Transputer Orb, an ancient tribal artifact of immense, but mysterious powers. This task was placed upon us by the Elders of the Brutor clan themselves and we have taken it very seriously. Then, a couple of months ago, disaster struck. Or should I say thief. My youngest brother was on duty in the ceremonial hall that day. The blame for the theft has hit him hard. Many have ostracized him and he''s been but a shell of a man since that fateful day. The rest of our family clan fairs only marginally better. Falling out of favor with the tribal elders is something few Minmatars walk away from unscathed.
I have made it my quest to track down the thief and retrieve the Transputer Orb. My trail has led me here to Traun, where I have reasons to believe the thief may be hiding. In many ways it''s the perfect hiding place; with all this warring going on it''s easy to cover one''s trail. And that''s exactly what this blasted thief has done and the reason for me coming here to plead with the good Sisters. With the flood of refugees coming in there must be someone that has some information for me, but without the Sister''s help I can''t get it.
My family clan is counting on me to get results soon and I''m starting to feel the pressure. I''m willing to offer good rewards to those willing to help me, you included. One lead I have is a man called Jihar Okham. He''s a Ni-Kunni of disputable virtue and a renown peddler of information. The presence of Okham here in Traun where I believe the thief is hiding is too much of a coincidence. I know trying to get him to talk is an exercise in futility. But I have an idea of how to get the information out of him.
Like many Amarrians he has his head crammed full of implants and it''s his memory implants I''m especially interested in. If I get them relatively soon after his demise I have the means to retrieve data from them. It''s a big chance, but it''s the best hope I''ve got. I''ve been roaming the system for a week now and been getting nowhere. I will pay you well if you''re willing to help me. You can find Okham in a contested complex here in the system. A man of his standings is bound to travel with companions, well armed companions no doubt. So take care.' WHERE missionID=93410 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I got the information I needed from Okham''s implants. Not only did they confirm that the thief is indeed here in Traun, but pinpointed his whereabouts even. He''s hiding in the very complex you found Okham in, only deeper inside.
I''ve also tried to glimpse the identity of the thief and what Okham was doing here. Unfortunately, there''s been some irretrievable data corruption that makes it very hard to delve deep into the memories embedded in the implants. From what I can glean the thief is waiting for some mysterious collector to arrive with payment for the stolen Orb. Okham was acting as a middle man, which makes me believe this collector is an Amarrian. It wouldn''t surprise me at least, the Amarrians have plundered the cultural heritage of the Minmatars for centuries and they''re loath to stop even now that we''ve thrown them out.
This is all beside the point. The room the thief is hiding in is inaccessible to all but those with a special key to unlock the old acceleration gate leading to it. We need to find a key in order to gain entrance. There are numerous old bunkers in the complex left by the Nefantars in their hasty retreat. As the gate lock is dating from the same time one of the bunkers might hold something we could use. If you could find even just a partial key or a broken keycard I might be able to repair it. Most of the valuables in the bunkers have long since been cleaned out by scavengers and the Angel cartel, but look carefully and you might find something of interest. As you know, the place is swarming with Angel cartel pirates and other scum, so take care.' WHERE missionID=93411 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I hope you still have the keycard I gave you, for you''re going to need it if you want to go after the thief. I''ve been trying to get more information out of Okham''s head, but I haven''t struck gold yet. So I really have no idea what you should expect in that last room. But I''ve been hanging around this camp for some time now and a few morsels of information have come my way.
My initial thought was that the last room was full of Angel cartel, but that''s not entirely true. Sure, there''s probable plenty of them there, but from what I''ve heard there are also lot of Thukker nomads and Minmatar paramilitaries skulking in the place. I don''t know how those guys will react when you turn up, but I think you should expect hostilities rather than hospitality.
In any case, the thief is hiding somewhere in there, all alone from what I gather. But someone brave enough to enter the ceremonial hall on my home planet in broad daylight and steal our most cherished position is undoubtedly someone more than capable of fending for himself. So be extra careful. I hear he''s on a battleship, though I have no idea how the heck he managed to squeeze that in there. If you manage to bring me back the Transputer Orb I will reward you with a very rare BPC that my family clan owns.' WHERE missionID=93412 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='I am in charge of Urban Management''s annual census gathering operation here in Hjoramold. My team flies between settlements in every corner of the system and gathers information on the population count. Then we process this information and finally send it to our headquarters in Abudban along with our report.
Sounds like a pretty simple and straight forward job, eh? And in the more civilized areas of Republic space, it is. But out here you never know what can happen. Every year some disaster strikes, and this year is no exception.
Two of my team have gone missing in addition to one getting stranded in an asteroid belt on her way back, due to her ship breaking down. Needless to say, I need some help getting them back.
First I''d like you to go looking for Kardimo Palettan, one of the workers who went missing. He''s my cousin twice removed, and we''ve known each other since we were kids. I would be terribly unhappy if something has happened to him.
He was on duty near Hjoramold X, collecting census data from some of the bio-dome settlements on the moons there, when he was beset by local thugs. We have a very strict policy here in Urban Management to stay well clear of all pirate infested areas, so we weren''t expecting this. Seems one of the local gangs, calling themselves the ''Maru Rebels'', thought Kardimo was trespassing on their territory and decided to punish him. I just hope he''s still alive. I suggest you scour the area around Hjoramold X''s moons, hopefully the Maru will have a base there somewhere. If you find him or any clues leading to him, then return to me for your reward.' WHERE missionID=93423 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Look for a ''Maru Prison Facility'' near Hjoramold X''s moons, and rescue Kardimo Palettan.' WHERE missionID=93424 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='The other census worker who''s having problems is currently stranded on Hjoramold XIII due to an unexpected rogue drone attack. Those drones seem to be randomly attacking all travelers going to and from the planet. The pilots are so scared Kyra, the census taker, can''t even find a single one to transport her off XIII. I''d like you to eliminate this threat ASAP so that Kyra can finally get her ass back to base. Republic security forces are taking too damn long to get the job done.
The only thing I need you to do is destroy the Searcher Drone. That will render the drone squad unable to scan all areas around the planet and should allow travelers safe passage as long as they avoid the dust cloud the buggers have been hiding in.' WHERE missionID=93425 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Ah so it''s you, <Character>. You''ve made quite a name for yourself within the inncer circles of the Empire, I''m sure you will come in handy. I have a few tasks that need to be carried out a.s.a.p., in the name of Joint Harvesting. Acquiring mercenaries in these parts has been quite difficult to say the least, considering the locals absolutely despise us. Their ungratefulness is astounding, considering how well we treated them during our reign over the Minmatar territories.
Well enough of that, I''ll get to the point. We had a convoy incoming from the Amarrian territories to one of our plantations in Barkrik when disaster struck. A group of vile ''freedom fighter'' terrorists ambushed them as soon as they appeared out of hyper-jump within Barkrik. The escort ships managed to fend off the attackers, allowing the freighter to escape relatively unharmed. But due to the interference, it went a little off course and ended up crashing into an area of deadspace we call ''The Dustbowl''. It''s not far from here, and all travelers are advised to avoid it at all costs. What a stroke of bad luck for our convoy to end up in there!
Needless to say, we haven''t heard from it since. The Dustbowl is infested with rogue drones and criminals hiding from the law. No sane person without a bounty on his head ventures in there, it''s a virtual death trap. I''m certain our freighter has either been destroyed or so badly damaged that it can''t escape. I want you to fly in there and investigate, if you find the freighter bring back anything you can salvage from it to me. And don''t speak a word of your findings to anyone! This is top secret business.' WHERE missionID=93458 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='The slaves you brought back in your last mission are almost all injured, some critically. We need medical supplies here ASAP, I don''t even dare move them to the plantation in this state. I don''t know how long some of them will last, so time is of the essence here. If you''re fast, I''ll give you a hefty bonus.
I couldn''t come up with the required medical supplies fast enough, so you''ll have to find them on your own. I suggest looking at the market in this or neighboring regions.' WHERE missionID=93459 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Although it looks like we will save most of the injured slaves you brought back in a previous mission, the current number of them is insufficient to satisfy the plantation overseer. Plus many of the ones that are getting better won''t be ready for work for some time.
Now I know we have an oversupply of slaves in Hjoramold currently, the Joint Harvesting plantations there don''t really need so many workers. They''ve agreed to supply us with an extra 50 slaves from their own stock. If you could just bring them here, past the Minmatar customs officials undetected, I''ll reward you well.' WHERE missionID=93460 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Ok the assignment is simple, but easier said than done. One of our hidden plantations within Barkrik has been infiltrated by the Freedom Fighter terrorist organization! They somehow managed to follow me there undetected while I transported the slaves you ferried here in your last mission to the plantation premises. A very devious plan of theirs ...
The last I heard the security defenses around the plantation had been overwhelmed. The plantation itself is hidden deep within an asteroid belt within deadspace, it will take them a while to reach it. Hopefully this will give you enough time to intercept their forces before they destroy all of our structures there! Defend our control tower at all costs! Succeed in this task and you will be well rewarded.' WHERE missionID=93461 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Why, hello to you stranger. It''s good to see a friendly face out here. Or at least someone not shooting at me. I''m Dr. Tikrest, by the way. Some call me Ramakell, but I prefer to be called the Professor. In case you haven''t heard of my work, I''m a renown sociologist.
So, what is a famous and handsome sociologist such as me doing out here in the middle of nowhere, you might be asking yourself? I don''t want to befuddle you with all the technical terminology of my trade, so let me put it simply. I have a reason to believe that a mysterious human civilization lived here in the Ani constellation thousands and thousands of years ago. Yes! I know it''s hard to believe, but a famous and intelligent person such as me wouldn''t make such a claim unless I was absolutely sure. A few of my more narrow-minded colleagues have scorned this idea of mine, so I''m out here to prove them wrong.
What I''m going to do is build an immense radio antenna capable of detecting the most miniscule signals from deep space. My theory is that such a powerful civilization as this one presumably was must have used some pretty powerful communication devices. Well, there still might be some fractions of signals left out there floating in space, waiting for someone renown and brilliant like me to pick them up.
Unfortunately, my work hasn''t launched under the most auspicious of portents. On my very first day out here, I was set upon by a brigand of the most obnoxious and foul-mouthed nature. Neither my illustrious career nor my most eloquent rhetoric sufficed to fend him off and he took off with my portable power generator. The scoundrel was flying a frigate, but he might be anywhere in the constellation by now. Damn Angels! What is the world coming to when renown and charming sociologists like me can''t go about their business without having some young punks and upstarts harassing them? Not to mention making lout and insidious remarks that are totally unfounded. The nerve of these pirates! Well, I wont stand for it. I''m not only renown, but also wealthy. I''ll pay you good money for hunting down that punk and bring me back my portable power generator.' WHERE missionID=93491 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Allow me to congratulate you once more on retrieving that power generator for me. It is invaluable for my work here. Your efficiency might almost suffice to make you a passable sociologist one day. But enough about that.
As I''ve already explained to you, I need to build an immense antenna to have any hope of catching a glimpse into past. To my frustration, the pitiful antennas available on the market are nowhere near being sufficient to meet my needs. But a renown and resourceful sociologist like me doesn''t let a little fact like that stop him. I''ve already placed an order with the firm Boundless Creations for them to custom make an antenna for me. It is being built at their factory over in the Hek system. Their work has progressed at an admiring rate, but they refuse to deliver it to me here. So I''m in need of a courier to fetch me my antenna. Of course, a renown and respected man such as myself can''t be bothered with such a trivial matter. But if you are interested, I will give you good money. I''ve learnt that when dealing with independent pilots such as yourself, money will convince people to do most anything.' WHERE missionID=93492 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='This is all coming together nicely, I must say. We have accomplished much, you and me, and now we''re on the brink of success that might change the world of sociology forever. Doesn''t it brighten your otherwise mundane existence to be a part, albeit a small one, in something as great as this? No need to thank me though, for a renown and modest sociologist such as me, fame and success is all it takes to fuel what little vanity I have.
But we''re not quite there yet. I''m still in need of a good signal amplifier to work alongside my new antenna. The one I brought was nowhere near up to the task and literally melted when I started feeding it the signals from the antenna. Luckily, one of my former students is in the Republic Fleet and is stationed here in Ani. It''s sad really, he''s very talented and had a brilliant and cozy career in sociology ahead of him. But no, he had to play the hero and go join the military, the fool.
Well, his loss is my gain now. I heard from him that after one of the many unsuccessful Republic invasions into the contested complex in Traun, he noticed one of his fallen comrades leaving behind a Republic amplifier. With a little bit of modification, that piece of equipment would be perfect for my purposes. If you hurry you might be able to get a hold of the amplifier before someone else scoops it up. I don''t know where it is exactly, but I gather from my ex-student that they were trying to force their way into the inner-most room of the complex when they beat a retreat. So have a look around that area. History waits for no man, renown sociologists or not, so to entice you into putting a step on it I''ll offer you a solid BPC as a reward for a job well done.' WHERE missionID=93493 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');

-- +migrate Down
-- (briefings stay)
